.TH GETLOGIN 3
.SH NAME
getlogin \- get login name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B char *getlogin(void);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Getlogin
returns a pointer to
the login name
as found in
.IR /etc/utmp .
It may be used
in conjunction
with
.I getpwnam
to locate the correct
password file entry
when the same userid
is shared by several
login names.
.PP
If
.I getlogin
is called within a process
that is not attached to a
typewriter, it returns NULL.
The correct procedure
for determining the login name
is to first call
.I getlogin
and if it fails,
to call
.IR getpwuid .
.SH FILES
/etc/utmp
.br
share/besm6/lib/libc.a, lib/libc/gen/getlogin.c
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getpwent(3), getgrent(3), utmp(5), ttyname(3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Returns NULL (0) if name not found.
.SH BUGS
The return values point to static data
whose content is overwritten by each call.
.PP
.B Note:
this routine stands on
.IR ttyslot (3),
which stands on
.IR ttyname (3),
which reads a directory with an ordinary
.IR read (2).
So it answers under this kernel and
.I not
under b6sim, whose
.I read
is the host's and refuses a directory.  Its failure path is what lib/test covers.
.SH BESM-6 NOTES
One v7 bug is fixed rather than carried: it wrote
.B "ubuf.ut_name[8] = ' '"
\- one past the end of the eight-character field \- as a sentinel before scanning
back over trailing blanks.  The scan is bounded now instead.

